    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.6.06-01",
      "block_type": "definition",
      "heading": "Stakeholders and sustainable use",
      "text": "Sustainable wildlife use maintains relevant populations, habitats and ecological functions while providing workable and appropriately shared human benefits. It is not simply a large animal count, a tourism label or a collection of permits. Government, NGOs, private enterprises, local authorities and local communities contribute different responsibilities and capacities. Their roles should be evaluated against explicit objectives and observed outcomes rather than listed as names without mechanisms.",
