      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.6.06-03",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Government also coordinates across boundaries and sectors. Wildlife movement, tourism, farming and infrastructure can involve competing objectives. A national decision may need local evidence and participation, while a local project may affect a wider ecosystem. Coordination matters because protecting one area can be undermined by incompatible action nearby. A declaration of cooperation is an input; evidence of aligned decisions and results is stronger support for success.",
