      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.6.06-04",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "NGOs can contribute research, training, technical advice, monitoring support and help with community capacity. A specialist organisation may link wildlife knowledge with practical ways of reducing conflict. Their effectiveness depends on the relevance and quality of assistance, continuity and whether intended users can apply it. Training attendance or money spent is not the same as demonstrated improvement in practice or ecological condition.",
