    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.6.06-05",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "The Cheetah Conservation Fund provides a named research-and-education example near Otjiwarongo. It illustrates that conservation work can extend beyond maintaining a park boundary to understanding animals and relationships with land users. Its existence should not be treated as proof that every farmer has received help or that a specified national trend improved. Use programme records for such claims rather than infer them from the organisation's name.",
