      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.6.06-06",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "NGO-supported monitoring needs suitable methods. A larger reported count can result from greater effort or improved detection rather than population growth. A training programme may improve recording, causing more incidents to be reported even if the underlying rate is unchanged. An evaluation should compare effort, definitions and coverage alongside the results. This is a reason for careful interpretation, not for dismissing monitoring as useless.",
