      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A private partnership should specify responsibilities, payments, employment arrangements and environmental requirements. Clear records allow participants to compare promises with delivery. A signed contract is relevant but does not establish that all terms were fulfilled. An evaluation might examine payments received, local sourcing, jobs, site condition and the way complaints are addressed. The appropriate evidence depends on the claim being judged.",
