      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.6.06-09",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Local authorities can influence land-use planning, infrastructure, waste services and coordination within their responsibilities. Their decisions can reduce some conflicts or create new pressures near wildlife areas. A road or waste facility should be assessed through siting, operation and effects, not simply construction. Jurisdiction matters: a local authority is not automatically responsible for every wildlife decision in the country.",
