      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.6.06-10",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Local service planning can reduce avoidable pressure where settlements and wildlife areas interact. Appropriate waste control can reduce pollution or attraction of animals to unsuitable places; land-use decisions can protect important connections. These measures need resources and cooperation. A collection schedule that is not delivered may leave the original problem unchanged. Maintenance and monitoring connect the authority's role to the intended environmental result.",
