    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.6.06-12",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Community perspectives can differ. A household employed in tourism may receive wages while another loses crops or livestock. Women, younger people, remote households or others may face different opportunities to participate. A management interview alone may miss those experiences. Suitable consultation and benefit records help identify distribution, while an anonymous or appropriately protected survey can gather views without assuming that one representative speaks for all.",
