    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.6.06-13",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Sustainable use needs an ecological balance as well as human arrangements. A hypothetical managed population begins with 100 animals, gains twenty through births and immigration and loses thirty through stated removals or deaths, with other changes absent. Closing stock is ninety. A permit allowing those removals does not change the balance. Judging longer-term sustainability needs recovery, age structure, habitat and other relevant evidence, not a label attached to the activity.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.6.06-1",
        "CL-6137-2.6.06-2",
