    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.6.06-14",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Count totals also depend on movement and detection. If animals leave a surveyed area, the local count can fall without an equal decline in the whole population. If effort increases, more may be seen without growth. Comparisons need the same area, season and suitable method or an account of differences. Those conditions make monitoring more useful and prevent a headline count from being treated as a complete management verdict.",
