    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.6.06-15",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Benefits should be measured at the level claimed. Revenue to a conservancy, wages to workers, payments to members and wildlife condition are separate outcomes. The June 2017 evaluation of Namibia’s Conservancy Support Activity, discussed in topic 2.3 Leisure and tourism, illustrates why enterprise or employment gains cannot automatically establish equal household income gains. A stakeholder evaluation should connect each role to the relevant result and retain the limits of the evidence.",
