    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.6.06-16",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Coordination can improve outcomes where roles complement one another: suitable government rules, NGO advice, private operating capacity, local services and community decisions can address different parts of the system. None of these contributions alone proves the whole system succeeds. A useful judgement identifies which role is functioning, what remains constrained and how monitoring or changes could address it.",
