    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.6.06-17",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Long-term success also needs continuity. Short grants or a favourable tourist season may support immediate work while leaving future operating costs unresolved. A management plan should consider finance, skills, resource recovery and changing environmental conditions. It should be possible to revise a measure when evidence shows harm or weak benefits. Adaptation based on monitoring is stronger than defending a method solely because it was previously approved.",
