    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.6.06-18",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A supported conclusion weighs wildlife condition, habitat, livelihoods and accountability against the stated aim. It can recognise a useful contribution while withholding a wider claim that lacks evidence. This is how stakeholder roles become an evaluation of sustainable management rather than a list of institutions or a claim that every intervention succeeds because conservation is its declared purpose.",
