    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.6.06-19",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "An enforcement evaluation can separate effort from outcome. More patrol days show activity, while fewer detected incidents may reflect deterrence, changed reporting or movement of illegal activity elsewhere. Compare patrol coverage, reporting methods and resource indicators before claiming a precise effect. A rise in reported incidents after improved recording does not automatically mean that the underlying rate worsened. The direction of the count must be interpreted through how it was produced.",
