    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.6.06-20",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A benefit-distribution account needs clear totals and recipients. Suppose a hypothetical management body receives N$100,000, spends N$40,000 on agreed conservation work, N$30,000 on recorded household benefits and retains N$30,000 for stated future obligations. The account identifies flows, not equal benefit to every member. Household-level records and agreed criteria are needed to assess fairness. The retained amount should not be called private profit or unexplained loss without evidence about ownership and obligations.",
