      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.6.06-22",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "The stakeholder contributions can be compared against the same criterion. If the aim is reducing livestock losses without undermining a predator population, examine both reported losses and suitable wildlife evidence. A measure reducing one total while causing an unassessed ecological cost has not established the combined goal. Joint monitoring and revision can address the trade-off more effectively than reporting each institution’s activity in isolation.",
