      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.6.06-24",
      "block_type": "cross_link",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "An extraction limit should be compared with recovery and other losses rather than treated as a biological result in itself. Suitable counts, habitat information and uncertainty inform the decision; compliance then concerns whether actual use follows the limit. An ecologically appropriate rule that is ignored and an inappropriate rule that is obeyed create different problems, both requiring attention.",
